hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1705","**\nNarrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr, who said: Narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: 'Umar ibn 'Ata' narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Rafi' narrated to us, who said: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, who said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, who said: 'Umar ibn 'Ata' ibn Abi al-Khuwar informed me.\n\nAnd narrated to us 'Ali ibn Sahl al-Ramli, who said: Al-Walid narrated to me, who said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to me, on the authority of 'Umar ibn 'Ata', who said: Nafi' ibn Jubayr sent me to al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid to ask him. So I asked him, and he said: \Yes"","" I prayed the Friday prayer in the *maqsurah* with Mu'awiyah. When he finished the prayer"","" I stood up to pray. So he sent for me"","" and I came to him. He said: 'If you pray the Friday prayer"","" do not connect it to another prayer unless you leave the mosque or speak. For the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded that.'\""\n\nAnd Ibn Rafi' and 'Abd al-Rahman said: \""He commanded that a prayer should not be connected to another prayer until you leave or speak.\""\n\nAbu Bakr said: This 'Umar ibn 'Ata' ibn Abi al-Khuwar is *thiqah* (trustworthy). The other one is 'Umar ibn 'Ata'"","" about whom our companions spoke due to his poor memory. Ibn Jurayj narrated from both of them.\n\n---"""""
